From: Feng Zhang <feng@radxa.com>
Date: Tue, 2 Dec 2025 07:31:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] aic8800: build with the vendor packager's own log level default (LOGERROR)

Ported to radxa-pkg/aic8800 5.0+git20260123.5f7be68d-8. The measurements below
were taken on the previous pin, 4.0+git20250410.b99ca8b6-5; file:line references
are to the 5.0 tag.

Measured on the board, one cold boot, 2026-08-23: 995 kernel
lines, 384 of them from this driver -- 39 % of the boot -- and `dmesg -x` puts
every single one of the 384 at KERN_WARNING, although the text calls itself
"AICWFDBG(LOGINFO)". The rest of the system in that same boot: 467 info, 99 warn,
16 notice, 8 debug, 3 err. Setting aicwf_dbg_level=0 at runtime dropped a WiFi
re-association from ~40 kernel lines to 5, of which 0 were AICWFDBG.

Why they are warnings, not info. AICWFDBG() assembles its own format string and
gives it no KERN_ prefix:

    #define AICWF_LOG "AICWFDBG("
    #define AICWFDBG(level, args, arg...)   \
    do {    \
        if (aicwf_dbg_level & level) {  \
            printk(AICWF_LOG#level")\t" args, ##arg); \
        }   \
    } while (0)

-- src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/aicwf_debug.h:17-24, and the
same macro in aic_load_fw/aicwf_debug.h. A printk() whose format
carries no KERN_ level is emitted at default_message_loglevel
(kernel/printk/printk.c:67, via include/linux/printk.h:49 ->
CONFIG_MESSAGE_LOGLEVEL_DEFAULT), which is 4 = KERN_WARNING both by kernel default
(lib/Kconfig.debug:75-79) and in our .config. "LOGINFO" is this driver's private
name for a gate bit in aicwf_dbg_level, never a syslog priority; the two were
never connected. So the priority cannot be fixed from the outside, and a
`loglevel=` on the command line silences the whole system or nothing.

What the level means. src/.../aic8800_fdrv/aicwf_debug.h:6-12 -- LOGERROR 0x1,
LOGINFO 0x2, LOGTRACE 0x4, LOGDEBUG 0x8, LOGDATA 0x10, LOGSTEER 0x20, LOGFW 0x200
(the last two are new in 5.0 and absent from aic_load_fw's copy) -- and the macro
tests `aicwf_dbg_level & level`, so it is a bitmask, not a threshold. The two
modules carry two separate variables with two different compiled-in defaults:
aic8800_fdrv 0x203 = LOGERROR|LOGINFO|LOGFW (rwnx_main.c:551) and aic_load_fw
0xf = LOGERROR|LOGINFO|LOGDEBUG|LOGTRACE (aic_bluetooth_main.c:23).

LOGFW gates one call site, rwnx_rx_handle_print() (rwnx_msg_rx.c:1757), which
prints the firmware's own log text when fwlog_en is set. With the bit off those
lines are not printed; the pr_err("FWLOG-OVFL: ...") just above it, taken when
fwlog_en is unset, is not gated and still prints.

This patch is not ours. It is debian/patches/fix-Lower-the-debugging-log-level.patch
by Feng Zhang <feng@radxa.com>, 2025-12-02, taken from the SAME pinned tree we
build (AIC8800_COMMIT df4c783b663eba1956579c681acd5e45f25c671d, listed in
debian/patches/series; its revision in that tag drops LOGFW as well) with the
PCIE and SDIO hunks dropped because we build neither. We miss it only because stage_fetch_wifi clones the git tree and applies
our patches, and never runs the packaging's quilt series -- so we build the raw
vendor source where Radxa's own package does not.

Measured against a board that runs Radxa's package: on the vendor Debian install
of an A7S, `cat /sys/module/aic8800_fdrv/parameters/aicwf_dbg_level` and the same
for aic_load_fw both read 1, with no modprobe.d entry anywhere on that system --
i.e. that value is the compiled-in default this patch restores, and it has been
in service there for months.

Effect, counted against the boot log of 2026-08-15
(418 AICWFDBG lines):
409 LOGINFO and 5 LOGDEBUG stop being emitted, 4 LOGERROR remain. Nothing that
reports a fault is lost: LOGERROR (0x1) stays set, and every genuine error path
in the driver uses it. Raising it again needs no rebuild --
`module_param(aicwf_dbg_level, int, 0660)` on both modules, so
/etc/modprobe.d/*.conf, a modprobe argument, or a write to
/sys/module/<mod>/parameters/aicwf_dbg_level all work at any time.

Side effect that matters here beyond noise: at LOGINFO the driver prints the SSID
in clear text on every association --
"rwnx_send_sm_connect_req ... connect to <ssid>(<len>) channel:<mhz> auth_type:<n>"
(rwnx_msg_tx.c:3832) and "cfg80211_unlink <ssid>" (rwnx_msg_rx.c:1171 and :1178).
Both are LOGINFO, so both go away with this patch; the remaining SSID prints in
the driver are LOGDEBUG (rwnx_msg_rx.c:780, rwnx_main.c:3395,
aicwf_wext_linux.c:990) and are off at this default too. That takes a live network
name out of every dmesg, screenshot and log this project attaches to a report.

Rejected alternative: teaching AICWFDBG a real KERN_ prefix (token-paste a
per-level AICWF_KERN_##level into the format). It is a two-file change and every
one of the 1585 call sites in the 5.0 tag passes a bare LOGxxx token, so it would work -- but it
fixes only the priority. The 409 lines and the SSID would still be there, just at
KERN_INFO, and it would be a delta of our own to carry forward at every vendor
bump instead of a line the vendor already maintains.

Note: aic_load_fw/aic_bluetooth_main.c uses CRLF line endings, so this patch
carries CR bytes. Keep it byte-exact.

